{
 "_note": "Media manifest. Same constraint as the data manifest: no build step and no directory listing, so every file is enumerated. preloadGroup controls what is fetched before the first frame ('boot'), what is fetched on chapter entry ('chapter1'/'chapter2'), and what streams on demand ('lazy'). The visual direction is set (concept/visual-design-principles.md). Every building has an on/off/broken render with the floorY its figures stand on (asset-production-spec \u00a72.1); animated rooms add an '<id>-on-anim' strip (frames side by side, played while on), and every other room adds an '<id>-dim' frame the renderer flickers to (\u00a72.5). A render whose contents a person can stand behind \u2014 a stair rail, cell bars, a table, a desk \u2014 also carries an '<id>-fg' cut of just those pixels, which the renderer draws over the figures (tools/cutForeground.mjs).",
